@startuml rank-regime-replay
' ============================================================================
' RankRegime replay drop-rule — the SAFETY-CRITICAL decision a recovering
' reader makes for EVERY WAL record, keyed on the file/segment's rank_regime
' (header byte 28) and whether the record carries a durable CommitRank.
' Source of truth:
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/wal/header.rs   (RankRegime { Owned=0, Overlay=1 })
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/recovery.rs     (reconcile_lww / generation_of /
'                                               the `RankRegime::Overlay => continue` drop)
' Color key:  amber #FFE0B2 = control / regime decision (frontier)
'             green #C8E6C9 = KEEP — the record contributes to recovered state
'             red   #FFCDD2 = DROP — the record is a two-append orphan, discarded
'             grey  #ECEFF1 = terminal / infrastructure
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
  DiamondBorderColor #F9A825
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFE0B2
}

title RankRegime replay drop-rule — applied per record, generation_of(lsn) = rank.unwrap_or(lsn)

start
:read next durable WAL record\n(lsn, record);

if (does this record carry a\ndurable **CommitRank**?) then (yes — RANKED)
  #C8E6C9:**KEEP** (generation = its CommitRank generation)\nthe op committed: its visibility CAS won AND\nthe rank was durably bound before the ack;
  note right #C8E6C9
    A ranked record is KEPT regardless of regime.
    Recovery stamps generation_of(lsn) = rank, and
    reconciles per term by MAX (generation, lsn) so
    LSN-ordered replay == CAS-order committed state.
  end note
else (no — UNRANKED)
  if (header **rank_regime** of this\nfile/segment?) then (Owned = 0)
    #C8E6C9:**KEEP** in LSN order\n(generation = lsn);
    note right #C8E6C9
      Owned / legacy / base / vocab producer:
      NO record is ever ranked, so every unranked
      record is a confirmed in-order append.
      generation_of(lsn) = lsn → stable LSN replay
      (byte-for-byte the pre-fix behavior).
    end note
  else (Overlay = 1)
    #FFCDD2:**DROP** — `continue` (skip the record)\nit is a **two-append orphan**;
    note right #FFCDD2
      Overlay producer: every CONFIRMED op carries a
      CommitRank. An unranked record is the gap between
      the data append and the (never-written) rank — a
      crash landed in the two-append window, so the op
      was NEVER acknowledged. Keeping it would RESURRECT
      a write that no caller ever saw succeed.
      THIS IS THE SAFETY-CRITICAL RULE.
    end note
  endif
endif

:emit the kept op (or nothing for a dropped /\nno-op record) into the (generation, lsn) merge;
stop

legend right
| Color | Outcome |
|<#FFE0B2>| regime decision |
|<#C8E6C9>| KEEP (recovered) |
|<#FFCDD2>| DROP (orphan) |
endlegend
@enduml
